.TH "tum\-check" "1" "" "" "tmux\-borrow Manual"
.SS NAME
\f[B]tum\-check\f[R] \[em] list orphans (host dead, utility alive)
.SS SYNOPSIS
\f[B]tum check\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]tum check\f[R] \f[B]\-h\f[R] | \f[B]\[en]help\f[R]
.SS DESCRIPTION
List orphans \[em] managed panes whose \f[CR]host\f[R] points at a pane
id that is no longer in \f[CR]list\-panes \-a\f[R] (the host pane died
but the utility pane is still alive).
Orphans are marked \f[CR]!\f[R] and left in place; there is no
auto\-action and no proactive hook on pane death.
.PP
Detection is lazy: it happens when you run \f[CR]tum check\f[R] (or
\f[CR]tum ls\f[R]), not when the host dies.
To clear an orphan, re\-borrow it (which re\-binds it to the current
host) or close it.
A fully\-dead pane \[em] utility gone too \[em] needs no handling: its
state died with it.
.SS OPTIONS
.IP \[bu] 2
\f[B]\-h\f[R], \f[B]\[en]help\f[R] Print a short synopsis (the SYNOPSIS
and EXAMPLES sections of this page) and exit.
For bare \f[B]tum\f[R], list every subcommand.
.SS EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
tum check                # list orphans: host dead, utility alive
# bound to  t g c  in the shipped tum\-bindings.conf
.EE
